WEBVTT

00:00:00.809 --> 00:00:03.180
about the author.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:12.372
Robert Louis Stevenson was born in Edinburgh, Scotland, on 13 November 1850.

00:00:12.432 --> 00:00:23.877
He was not a strong child and was often ill, but he liked the stories about adventures and pirates which his father told him.

00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:29.400
In the late 1860s he went to Edinburgh University.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:36.262
At first he decided to study engineering because his father was an engineer.

00:00:36.322 --> 00:00:45.265
But Stevenson soon understood that he was not happy with his choice and decided to study law.

00:00:45.325 --> 00:00:53.767
It was during this time that he became very interested in literature and he began writing stories.

00:00:53.827 --> 00:00:58.989
many of these were published in magazines.

00:00:59.049 --> 00:01:07.773
In 1876, Stevenson started travelling through Belgium and France, where he met Fanny Osborne.

00:01:07.832 --> 00:01:14.646
She was American, eleven years older than himself and a mother of two children.

00:01:14.706 --> 00:01:20.762
They fell in love immediately, but they did not get married until 1880.

00:01:20.822 --> 00:01:27.610
After their marriage, they went to live in Scotland with her son, Lloyd.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:34.304
One day, Stevenson started telling Lloyd a story about pirates.

00:01:34.363 --> 00:01:41.579
This was the beginning of one of Stevenson's most famous stories, Treasure Island.

00:01:41.639 --> 00:01:54.952
This exciting adventure story about pirates and treasure became very popular with children and adults all over the world, and Stevenson became a famous writer.

00:01:55.012 --> 00:02:04.332
In 1886, he wrote his most famous novel, The Strange Case of Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde.

00:02:04.392 --> 00:02:13.451
This tells the story of a doctor who drinks a special potion and develops a horrible new personality.

00:02:13.511 --> 00:02:25.240
His other important novels include Kidnapped, 1886, The Black Arrow, 1888 and The Master of Balantry, 1889.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:38.646
In 1888, Stevenson was still ill, and he felt that the cold, wet, Scottish weather was not good for him.

00:02:38.706 --> 00:02:43.148
So the family decided to travel to the South Pacific.

00:02:43.208 --> 00:02:52.181
They spent two years travelling and visited the islands of Hawaii, Tahiti, Samoa and many others.

00:02:52.241 --> 00:02:59.067
The warm weather helped Stevenson a lot, so the family decided to live in Samoa.

00:02:59.127 --> 00:03:05.626
Stevenson liked Samoa and the people very much and they liked him too.

00:03:05.686 --> 00:03:13.592
He studied the life and customs of these people and started writing numerous stories set on the islands.

00:03:13.652 --> 00:03:22.225
Some of these stories were published in a collection called Island Nights Entertainment's 1893.

00:03:22.285 --> 00:03:29.307
Stevenson died in December 1894 in his home in Samoa.

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:32.308
He was only 44 years old.

00:03:32.368 --> 00:03:38.542
The people of Samoa buried him on top of Mount Veer.

00:03:38.602 --> 00:03:52.662
Chapter 1 The Letter The bell of Mothouse Castle at Tunstall rang loudly one spring afternoon.

00:03:52.722 --> 00:03:57.125
The people of the village looked up at the castle.

00:03:57.185 --> 00:03:58.676
What's happening?

00:03:58.736 --> 00:03:59.936
Asked one man.

00:03:59.956 --> 00:04:03.027
I don't know, said another.

00:04:03.087 --> 00:04:08.218
A messenger brought a letter for Sir Oliver Oates, the priest, half an hour ago.

00:04:08.278 --> 00:04:10.759
It was from Sir Daniel Brackley.

00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:14.280
But why is the bell ringing?

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.781
Asked an old man.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:23.084
Suddenly, a handsome young man appeared on his grey horse.

00:04:23.144 --> 00:04:30.018
He was about eighteen years old, and had brown hair and blue eyes.

00:04:30.078 --> 00:04:33.309
He had a bow and arrow on his back.

00:04:33.368 --> 00:04:39.920
His name was Richard Shelton, and he was Sir Daniel's ward.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:46.952
Richard Shelton looked at the people around him and said, There will be a big battle soon.

00:04:47.012 --> 00:04:50.002
Sir Daniel wants everyone to fight.

00:04:50.062 --> 00:04:52.324
Another battle!

00:04:52.383 --> 00:04:54.135
cried an angry woman.

00:04:54.195 --> 00:04:56.126
This is terrible.

00:04:56.186 --> 00:05:02.830
Our men go and die in battles, and their wives and children are hungry.

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:09.362
We pay high taxes to Sir Daniel, and we don't have any money for food.

00:05:09.422 --> 00:05:13.234
Said a young mother, with three small children.

00:05:13.294 --> 00:05:16.516
Who is Sir Daniel fighting for today?

00:05:16.576 --> 00:05:18.260
Asked a tall man.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:20.344
Lancaster or York?

00:05:20.404 --> 00:05:27.548
I'm sorry, I don't know," said Richard, and his face became red.

00:05:27.608 --> 00:05:35.120
Sir Daniel Brackley was not a loyal man, and the people did not like him.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:38.842
He seems to always change his mind.

00:05:38.902 --> 00:05:45.674
Sometimes he fought for Lancaster, and sometimes he fought for York.

00:05:45.734 --> 00:05:50.014
A big man on a black horse appeared.

00:05:50.074 --> 00:05:55.026
It was Bennett Hatch, Sir Daniel's best friend.

00:05:55.086 --> 00:06:01.529
He was about forty and had dark hair and an unfriendly face.

00:06:01.589 --> 00:06:08.282
All of the men in the village must go to Mote House Castle and get ready for the battle!

00:06:08.342 --> 00:06:10.112
Hatch cried.

00:06:10.172 --> 00:06:16.598
Then Hatch looked at Richard and said, Let's go to Nick Appleyard's house.

00:06:16.658 --> 00:06:19.874
When they arrived, Hatch said.

00:06:19.934 --> 00:06:28.200
Nick Appleyard, you must go and defend Mothouse Castle, because Sir Daniel is going to Keckley to fight.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:38.037
While the two men were talking, a black arrow suddenly hit Nick Appleyard in the back and killed him.

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:39.308
Oh no!

00:06:39.368 --> 00:06:40.559
cried Richard.

00:06:40.619 --> 00:06:42.280
Appleyard is dead.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:45.392
Someone in the forest shot this black arrow.

00:06:45.452 --> 00:06:46.340
Look!

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.529
There's a message on the arrow, said Hatch.

00:06:49.589 --> 00:06:51.819
What does it say, Richard?

00:06:51.879 --> 00:07:00.532
Richard took the arrow and read, for Appleyard, from John, to make things right.

00:07:00.592 --> 00:07:02.872
What a strange message.

00:07:02.932 --> 00:07:04.752
It's dangerous here.

00:07:04.812 --> 00:07:08.113
Let's go to the church, said Hatch.

00:07:08.173 --> 00:07:13.214
There were about twenty men on their horses outside the church.

00:07:13.274 --> 00:07:15.572
They were ready to fight.

00:07:15.632 --> 00:07:20.782
Sir Daniel will be pleased with these brave men, said Hatch.

00:07:20.842 --> 00:07:23.844
Look at the church door, said Richard.

00:07:23.904 --> 00:07:25.684
There's a letter on it.

00:07:25.744 --> 00:07:31.258
A letter on the church door, said Sir Oliver, surprised.

00:07:31.318 --> 00:07:36.172
He was the priest of the village, and Sir Daniel's good friend.

00:07:36.232 --> 00:07:39.904
Young Richard, please read it.

00:07:39.964 --> 00:07:45.358
Richard took the letter off the door, and read it aloud.

00:07:45.418 --> 00:07:48.002
I have four black arrows.

00:07:48.062 --> 00:07:51.244
The first arrow killed Apple Yard.

00:07:51.304 --> 00:07:57.830
The next one will kill Bennett Hatch because he burnt Grimstone House.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:05.276
Another arrow is for Sir Oliver Oates because he killed Sir Harry Shelton.

00:08:05.335 --> 00:08:09.290
Sir Daniel will get the fourth arrow.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:13.435
From John of the Greenwood and his men.

00:08:13.495 --> 00:08:19.631
P.S., remember we have other arrows for your men.

00:08:19.691 --> 00:08:22.903
We live in a terrible world.

00:08:22.962 --> 00:08:24.293
I'm a good man.

00:08:24.313 --> 00:08:29.746
I did not kill Sir Harry Shelton, cried Sir Oliver Oates.

00:08:29.806 --> 00:08:35.780
We know you're a good, honest man, Sir Oliver, said Hatch.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:41.154
Then he whispered something in Sir Oliver's ear and looked at Richard.

00:08:41.214 --> 00:08:44.788
Sir Harry Shelton was Richard's father.

00:08:44.848 --> 00:08:49.081
Richard saw this, but he said nothing.

00:08:49.141 --> 00:08:56.786
I must write a letter to Sir Daniel and tell him what happened, said Sir Oliver.

00:08:56.846 --> 00:09:05.772
When the letter was ready, he said, Richard, take this important letter to Sir Daniel immediately.

00:09:05.832 --> 00:09:10.872
Be careful on the road because it can be very dangerous.

00:09:10.932 --> 00:09:15.731
Richard took the letter and went to get his horse.

00:09:15.791 --> 00:09:18.411
Hatch followed him.

00:09:18.471 --> 00:09:21.302
Richard, he said quietly.

00:09:21.362 --> 00:09:24.622
You're a brave, honest young man.

00:09:24.682 --> 00:09:26.212
Listen to me.

00:09:26.272 --> 00:09:28.693
Be careful of Sir Daniel.

00:09:28.753 --> 00:09:33.654
Don't trust him and don't trust Sir Oliver.

00:09:33.714 --> 00:09:36.284
They're dangerous men.

00:09:36.344 --> 00:09:40.132
Richard was surprised and started thinking.

00:09:40.192 --> 00:09:43.260
Thank you, my friend," he said.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:49.732
Then he got on his grey horse and galloped away.

00:09:49.792 --> 00:10:04.045
CHAPTER II JOHN MATCHAM Sir Daniel Brackley sat next to the fire at the sign of the sun in in Keckley.

00:10:04.105 --> 00:10:07.468
He was a tall man of about forty.

00:10:07.528 --> 00:10:12.391
he was born and had a big nose and black eyes.

00:10:12.451 --> 00:10:19.613
He collected taxes all day, and now he was thinking about how he could make more money.

00:10:19.673 --> 00:10:25.744
Sir Daniel was a very greedy man and did many bad things.

00:10:25.804 --> 00:10:30.186
A thin young boy was sitting near the door of the inn.

00:10:30.246 --> 00:10:34.282
He was very sad.

00:10:34.342 --> 00:10:42.332
The young boy was about thirteen and had blonde hair and blue eyes.

00:10:42.392 --> 00:10:47.758
He was wearing dirty old clothes and a big brown hat.

00:10:47.818 --> 00:10:52.384
Sir Daniel looked at him and laughed.

00:10:52.444 --> 00:10:56.316
You make me laugh, John.

00:10:56.376 --> 00:10:58.217
Don't laugh at me.

00:10:58.277 --> 00:10:59.688
Said John angrily.

00:10:59.748 --> 00:11:01.270
I don't like it.

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:03.622
Oh, let me laugh.

00:11:03.682 --> 00:11:04.993
Said Sir Daniel.

00:11:05.053 --> 00:11:08.006
I'll plan a good marriage for you.

00:11:08.066 --> 00:11:09.597
You'll see.

00:11:09.657 --> 00:11:13.640
And I'll make a lot of money with this marriage.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:15.292
Thought Sir Daniel.

00:11:15.352 --> 00:11:18.865
Lord Shorby will pay me well.

00:11:18.925 --> 00:11:22.878
The young boy went to sit down again.

00:11:22.938 --> 00:11:26.888
Some time later, Richard came into the inn.

00:11:26.948 --> 00:11:27.709
Ah!

00:11:27.769 --> 00:11:30.560
Richard, my brave boy!

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:31.951
Said Sir Daniel.

00:11:32.011 --> 00:11:34.142
Sit down and eat.

00:11:34.202 --> 00:11:37.243
You're probably hungry and thirsty.

00:11:37.303 --> 00:11:43.656
Here's an important letter from Sir Oliver, said Richard, giving him the letter.

00:11:43.716 --> 00:11:47.280
Sir Daniel read it, and he was worried.

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:52.396
Richard, the letter on the church door is a lie.

00:11:52.456 --> 00:11:53.717
Said Sir Daniel.

00:11:53.777 --> 00:11:57.460
Sir Oliver did not kill your poor father.

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:04.485
Ellis Duckworth killed your father, but he escaped and we never found him.

00:12:04.545 --> 00:12:07.468
Did this happen at Motow's Castle?

00:12:07.528 --> 00:12:11.470
asked Richard, looking into Sir Daniel's eyes.

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:15.464
It happened between Motow's and Holywood.

00:12:15.524 --> 00:12:17.056
Answered Sir Daniel.

00:12:17.116 --> 00:12:20.058
But now, sit down and eat.

00:12:20.118 --> 00:12:26.671
I must answer Sir Oliver's letter, and then you can take it back to him in Tunstall.

00:12:26.732 --> 00:12:32.284
While Richard was eating, he heard a soft voice near his ear.

00:12:32.344 --> 00:12:37.786
Please don't turn around, but tell me the way to Holywood.

00:12:37.846 --> 00:12:43.149
Take the road by the old church, Richard Wispon.

00:12:43.209 --> 00:12:45.270
He did not turn around.

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:48.982
But he saw the boy leave the inn quietly.

00:12:49.042 --> 00:12:53.156
Take this message to Tunstle immediately.

00:12:53.216 --> 00:12:55.590
said Sir Daniel to Richard.

00:12:55.650 --> 00:13:00.975
Then he looked around the inn and said, Where is that girl?

00:13:01.035 --> 00:13:03.278
That boy, John.

00:13:03.338 --> 00:13:05.800
He left the inn about an hour ago.

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:06.992
Said Richard.

00:13:07.052 --> 00:13:08.722
I must find him!"

00:13:08.782 --> 00:13:10.193
cried Sir Daniel.

00:13:10.253 --> 00:13:17.174
He turned to one of his men, and said, James, take six men and go and find that boy.

00:13:17.234 --> 00:13:20.195
Richard left the inn with the message.

00:13:20.255 --> 00:13:26.346
He rode his horse all night, and early the next morning he was near a marsh.

00:13:26.406 --> 00:13:30.288
In the marsh, he saw a young boy on his horse.

00:13:30.348 --> 00:13:32.842
But the horse was not moving.

00:13:32.902 --> 00:13:36.538
You're the boy from the inn, said Richard.

00:13:36.598 --> 00:13:38.639
I saw you last night.

00:13:38.699 --> 00:13:40.259
Yes, I am.

00:13:40.319 --> 00:13:41.150
He said.

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:45.221
I'm lost, and my horse hurt his leg in the marsh.

00:13:45.281 --> 00:13:47.131
Now he can't move.

00:13:47.191 --> 00:13:50.272
The poor horse, said Richard.

00:13:50.332 --> 00:13:53.373
I'm sorry, but I must kill it.

00:13:53.433 --> 00:13:55.214
Please get off.

00:13:55.274 --> 00:13:59.729
When the boy got off, he killed the horse.

00:13:59.789 --> 00:14:03.675
Can you help me go to Holywood, Master Shelton?

00:14:03.735 --> 00:14:04.896
Ask the boy.

00:14:04.956 --> 00:14:09.829
Yes, I can, said Richard, but who are you?

00:14:09.889 --> 00:14:12.350
Call me John Matcham.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:13.822
Said the boy.

00:14:13.882 --> 00:14:16.773
Why do you want to go to Holywood, John?

00:14:16.833 --> 00:14:18.004
Asked Richard.

00:14:18.064 --> 00:14:22.457
There's a kind friar at Holywood, and he'll protect me.

00:14:22.517 --> 00:14:23.718
Said John.

00:14:23.778 --> 00:14:25.409
Protect you?

00:14:25.469 --> 00:14:26.620
Asked Richard.

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:27.602
Yes.

00:14:27.662 --> 00:14:31.676
He'll protect me from Sir Daniel Brackley, said the boy.

00:14:31.736 --> 00:14:33.937
He's a very bad man.

00:14:33.997 --> 00:14:39.268
He took me from my home and gave me these dirty clothes to wear.

00:14:39.328 --> 00:14:43.980
But I know, Sir Daniel, said Richard, he's not an evil man.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:47.991
He's evil and greedy, believe me.

00:14:48.051 --> 00:14:49.181
Said the boy.

00:14:49.241 --> 00:14:51.402
One day you'll understand why.

00:14:51.422 --> 00:14:59.600
He was silent for a moment, and then said, I heard that you are going to get married soon.

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:00.501
What?

00:15:00.521 --> 00:15:02.682
I said Richard laughing.

00:15:02.742 --> 00:15:05.064
And who am I going to marry?

00:15:05.124 --> 00:15:06.655
Joanna Sedley.

00:15:06.715 --> 00:15:07.716
Said the boy.

00:15:07.776 --> 00:15:10.528
Sir Daniel planned the marriage.

00:15:10.588 --> 00:15:11.819
Oh!

00:15:11.879 --> 00:15:13.070
said Richard.

00:15:13.130 --> 00:15:15.332
And his face became red.

00:15:15.392 --> 00:15:17.773
But I don't know her.

00:15:17.833 --> 00:15:23.728
Suddenly they heard a noise and saw Sir Daniel's seven men on the hill.

00:15:23.788 --> 00:15:55.038
said Daniel's men cried the boy they're looking for me don't worry I'll take you to Hollywood I promise said Richard get on my horse quickly John smiled at his new friend and together they galloped into the dark forest the walls of the roses There was civil war in England from 1455 to 1485.

00:15:55.098 --> 00:16:01.450
This was because of an argument between the families of York and Lancaster.

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:10.453
Each noble family at this time had a picture of an object which they used as a special symbol of their family.

00:16:10.513 --> 00:16:17.016
The Lancastrians had a red rose and the Yorkists had a white rose.

00:16:17.076 --> 00:16:21.350
This gave the name to the Wars of the Roses.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:35.046
Both the Yorkists and the Lancastrians were descendants of King Edward III, 1327 to 77, and both wanted to be King of England.

00:16:35.106 --> 00:16:43.042
In 1455, the King of England was Henry VI, a member of the Lancaster family.

00:16:43.102 --> 00:16:50.878
but the leader of the York family, John, Duke of York, also wanted to be king.

00:16:50.938 --> 00:16:58.662
The first battle was in 1455 at St. Albans, just north of London.

00:16:58.722 --> 00:17:04.115
The Yorkists won, but Henry VI was still king.

00:17:04.176 --> 00:17:07.695
Three years passed before the next battle.

00:17:07.754 --> 00:17:15.215
But between 1459 and 1461, there were eight more battles.

00:17:15.275 --> 00:17:24.939
The Yorkists won five of these, and finally, in 1461, there was a Yorkist king for the first time.

00:17:24.999 --> 00:17:31.110
Edward IV, 1461 to 70, 1471 to 83.

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:46.138
After Edward IV's death in 1483, the heir to the throne was the eldest son, Edward V, but he was still a child at this time.

00:17:46.198 --> 00:17:54.233
Edward IV's brother, the Duke of Gloucester, was the guardian of both the boy and his younger brother.

00:17:54.294 --> 00:18:02.956
The Duke also wanted to be king, so he decided to put the boys in prison in the Tower of London.

00:18:03.016 --> 00:18:11.890
People believed that they were killed soon after their arrival, and the Duke became King Richard III.

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:16.954
There were 17 battles during the Thirty Years of War.

00:18:17.014 --> 00:18:23.881
These happened all over England, in the North, South, East and West.

00:18:23.941 --> 00:18:34.546
On 22 August 1485, Henry Tudor, a descendant of the house of Lancaster, won the final battle.

00:18:34.606 --> 00:18:39.279
Richard III, the last York king, was killed.

00:18:39.339 --> 00:18:44.302
Henry Tudor then became King Henry VII.

00:18:44.362 --> 00:18:52.616
A year later, he married Elizabeth of York, and the Lancaster and York families would join together.

00:18:52.676 --> 00:19:01.851
To show this, the white rose of York and the red rose of Lancaster became one red and white rose.

00:19:01.911 --> 00:19:12.384
This was called the Tudor Rose, as was the symbol of the Tudors, a new line of English kings and queens.

00:19:12.444 --> 00:19:19.176
Listening Activity Lawless?

00:19:19.236 --> 00:19:21.754
Isn't that food ready yet?

00:19:21.814 --> 00:19:23.460
Here you are, Ellis.

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:27.021
Freshly cooked eggs for the first time in a month.

00:19:27.082 --> 00:19:29.782
Well done, Lawless.

00:19:29.842 --> 00:19:31.973
Where did you get the eggs from?

00:19:32.033 --> 00:19:34.374
From a farmhouse near Catley.

00:19:34.434 --> 00:19:35.794
Don't worry, Ellis.

00:19:35.854 --> 00:19:38.895
The band of the Black Arrow has many friends.

00:19:38.955 --> 00:19:41.066
We will not be hungry.

00:19:41.126 --> 00:19:42.726
You're right, Lawless.

00:19:42.787 --> 00:19:44.997
We have many loyal friends.

00:19:45.057 --> 00:19:50.297
There are many people that hate Sir Daniel Brackley and want to help the band.

00:19:50.357 --> 00:19:53.766
They know Brackley is a cruel man.

00:19:53.826 --> 00:19:56.818
Just look what he did to your house, Ellis.

00:19:56.878 --> 00:20:03.291
Yes, my dear home burnt down by Bennett Hatch.

00:20:03.352 --> 00:20:07.014
Well, he will pay for it.

00:20:07.074 --> 00:20:11.416
Listen, Ellis, someone's coming through the forest.

00:20:11.476 --> 00:20:14.367
I think it must be Daniel Brackley's men.

00:20:14.427 --> 00:20:20.594
Quick, everyone, hide and get ready to attack.

00:20:20.654 --> 00:20:36.993
Chapter 3 Mote House Castle Richard and John rode through the dark forest of Tunstall, where the tall trees moved in the wind.

00:20:37.053 --> 00:20:41.644
They stopped when they found a big burnt house.

00:20:41.704 --> 00:20:45.595
This house looks like Grinstone, said Richard.

00:20:45.655 --> 00:20:46.866
Grinstone?

00:20:46.926 --> 00:20:47.786
asked John.

00:20:47.846 --> 00:20:48.999
What's that?

00:20:49.059 --> 00:20:54.806
It was Ellis Duckworth's house until Bennett Hatch burnt it down five years ago.

00:20:54.866 --> 00:20:58.648
It was a very beautiful house before the fire.

00:20:58.708 --> 00:21:03.802
Behind the house they saw some men sitting around a fire.

00:21:03.862 --> 00:21:09.575
They were wearing old dark clothes and each man had a bow and arrow.

00:21:09.635 --> 00:21:14.762
They were eating and talking like old friends and some were laughing.

00:21:14.822 --> 00:21:18.528
Suddenly, a man up a tall tree cried.

00:21:18.588 --> 00:21:21.840
I see seven of Sir Daniel's men coming here.

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:23.692
Is Sir Daniel with them?

00:21:23.752 --> 00:21:25.243
Asked a handsome man.

00:21:25.303 --> 00:21:27.434
No, I can't see him.

00:21:27.494 --> 00:21:29.776
An said the man on the tall tree.

00:21:29.836 --> 00:21:31.278
Let's attack them.

00:21:31.338 --> 00:21:32.939
Cried the handsome man.

00:21:32.999 --> 00:21:34.980
Go to your places quickly.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:40.955
I must go and tell Sir Daniel's men about the attack, said Richard to John.

00:21:41.015 --> 00:21:42.386
But why?

00:21:42.446 --> 00:21:44.536
Asked John, surprised.

00:21:44.596 --> 00:21:46.006
They're looking for me.

00:21:46.066 --> 00:21:48.567
You promised to take me to Holywood.

00:21:48.627 --> 00:21:50.458
You can't leave me now."

00:21:50.518 --> 00:21:53.279
You're right, John," said Richard.

00:21:53.339 --> 00:21:55.539
I'll take you to Holywood.

00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:58.451
Richard remembered his promise.

00:21:58.511 --> 00:22:03.884
The man in the forest took their bows and arrows and ran to their places.

00:22:03.944 --> 00:22:07.325
They started attacking Sir Daniel's men.

00:22:07.385 --> 00:22:14.334
When the attack was over, one of the men in the forest saw Richard and wanted to kill him.

00:22:14.394 --> 00:22:15.950
No, don't!

00:22:16.010 --> 00:22:17.921
cried the handsome man.

00:22:17.981 --> 00:22:23.622
It was Ellis Duckworth, the leader of the band of the Black Arrow.

00:22:23.683 --> 00:22:25.993
This boy is Harry's son.

00:22:26.053 --> 00:22:28.014
We mustn't hurt him.

00:22:28.074 --> 00:22:30.644
Bring him to me immediately.

00:22:30.704 --> 00:22:32.815
I want to talk to him.

00:22:32.875 --> 00:22:37.396
Richard heard him and said, oh no, let's run away from here, John.

00:22:37.456 --> 00:22:38.666
Quickly!

00:22:38.726 --> 00:22:44.090
The two boys ran to the top of the hill and two men followed them.

00:22:44.150 --> 00:22:47.896
John was tired, but he continued running.

00:22:47.956 --> 00:22:53.902
They soon reached another forest, and Richard said, no one is following us now.

00:22:53.962 --> 00:22:55.534
We're safe.

00:22:55.594 --> 00:22:59.838
I can't walk or run anymore, said John.

00:22:59.898 --> 00:23:01.770
I'm very tired.

00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:03.022
Tired?

00:23:03.082 --> 00:23:04.093
Said Richard.

00:23:04.153 --> 00:23:06.485
What kind of a boy are you?

00:23:06.545 --> 00:23:10.538
John looked at him and started crying.

00:23:10.598 --> 00:23:14.611
Oh, please don't cry, said Richard, smiling.

00:23:14.671 --> 00:23:16.412
Look, there's a river.

00:23:16.472 --> 00:23:19.424
Let's go and drink some cold water.

00:23:19.484 --> 00:23:25.410
Later, when it was dark, they fell asleep under a tree.

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:29.732
The next morning, they woke up and were hungry.

00:23:29.792 --> 00:23:32.414
But they had nothing to eat.

00:23:32.474 --> 00:23:36.466
Suddenly, they heard a noise coming from the forest.

00:23:36.527 --> 00:23:39.706
They saw a friar walking towards them.

00:23:39.766 --> 00:23:42.996
His head was covered with a big hood.

00:23:43.056 --> 00:23:47.038
He stopped near them and took off his hood.

00:23:47.098 --> 00:23:49.899
Sir Daniel cried, Richard.

00:23:49.959 --> 00:23:51.609
This is a surprise.

00:23:51.669 --> 00:23:53.289
What are you doing here?

00:23:53.350 --> 00:23:56.010
And why are you dressed like a friar?

00:23:56.070 --> 00:23:58.441
Richard said, Sir Daniel.

00:23:58.501 --> 00:24:01.382
We lost the battle against York.

00:24:01.442 --> 00:24:06.214
It was a terrible battle, and most of my men were killed.

00:24:06.274 --> 00:24:10.486
I am wearing friars' clothes so I can escape.

00:24:10.546 --> 00:24:14.558
Now I'm going home to Mote House Castle.

00:24:14.618 --> 00:24:18.659
Sir Daniel gave them both some bread and cheese.

00:24:18.719 --> 00:24:23.151
Richard and John ate quickly because they were very hungry.

00:24:23.211 --> 00:24:26.772
I'm surprised to see you two boys together.

00:24:26.832 --> 00:24:28.053
Said Sir Daniel.

00:24:28.113 --> 00:24:30.344
But now you're both coming with me.

00:24:30.364 --> 00:24:32.174
Do you understand?

00:24:32.234 --> 00:24:33.835
Very well, Sir Daniel.

00:24:33.895 --> 00:24:34.936
Said Richard.

00:24:34.996 --> 00:24:36.276
Yes, sir.

00:24:36.336 --> 00:24:38.898
said John quietly.

00:24:38.958 --> 00:24:44.702
Richard and John followed Sir Daniel, and they soon arrived at the castle.

00:24:44.762 --> 00:24:51.436
Before going in, John said, well, Richard, now we must say goodbye.

00:24:51.496 --> 00:24:52.958
But why?

00:24:53.018 --> 00:24:54.008
said Richard.

00:24:54.068 --> 00:24:56.650
We're both going to Motehouse Castle.

00:24:56.710 --> 00:25:00.337
We're good friends, and we can see each other all the time.

00:25:00.398 --> 00:25:04.544
You won't see me anymore," said John sadly.

00:25:04.604 --> 00:25:06.935
And I can't explain why.

00:25:06.995 --> 00:25:14.768
I must do what Sir Daniel says, but remember Richard, be careful of Sir Daniel.

00:25:14.827 --> 00:25:19.919
Richard did not like this mystery and wanted to know more.

00:25:19.979 --> 00:25:24.928
Goodbye, my young friend, said Richard sadly.

00:25:24.988 --> 00:25:34.491
Mote House Castle was a stone castle with a drawbridge, a moat and four tall towers.

00:25:34.551 --> 00:25:43.164
There were now only 22 men in the castle because a lot of them were killed during the last battle against York.

00:25:43.224 --> 00:25:50.838
These men were afraid of the band of the Black Arrow because the band lived in the forest near the castle.

00:25:50.898 --> 00:25:55.079
Richard went to his bedroom and closed the door.

00:25:55.139 --> 00:25:59.400
It was a big, cold room near the top of the castle.

00:25:59.460 --> 00:26:06.944
He did not have many things inside, just a large bed, a table, and chair.

00:26:07.004 --> 00:26:12.908
Richard liked the room because it was somewhere he could stay on his own and think.

00:26:12.968 --> 00:26:19.070
Now he went to sit on the bed so he could think about all the recent events.

00:26:19.130 --> 00:26:23.467
What's happening at Motaz Castle, he thought?

00:26:23.527 --> 00:26:26.983
Why can't I see my friend John Matcham anymore?

00:26:27.043 --> 00:26:31.016
Why is everyone telling me to be careful of Sir Daniel?

00:26:31.076 --> 00:26:33.707
Who is Joanna, sadly?

00:26:33.767 --> 00:26:36.908
How can I marry her if I don't know her?

00:26:36.969 --> 00:26:42.932
Richard was very confused and looked out of the small window in his room.

00:26:42.992 --> 00:26:49.718
He could see the big forest, and he started thinking about the letter from John of the Greenwood.

00:26:49.779 --> 00:26:54.113
The letter says, Sir Oliver killed my father, he thought.

00:26:54.173 --> 00:26:57.455
But Sir Daniel says, the letter is not true.

00:26:57.515 --> 00:27:00.758
He says Ellis Duckworth killed him.

00:27:00.818 --> 00:27:04.080
Did Ellis Duckworth really kill him?

00:27:04.140 --> 00:27:09.332
I don't believe Sir Daniel, because I think he's hiding something from me.

00:27:09.393 --> 00:27:11.204
But what?

00:27:11.264 --> 00:27:15.756
I want to know the truth, and must know the truth.

00:27:15.816 --> 00:27:20.738
And only Sir Daniel can answer my questions.

00:27:20.798 --> 00:27:31.534
Chapter 4 Joanna Sedley Someone knocked on Richard's door.

00:27:31.594 --> 00:27:34.498
It was Bennett Hatch.

00:27:34.558 --> 00:27:37.101
Good afternoon, Richard, he said.

00:27:37.161 --> 00:27:39.662
Sir Daniel wants to see you immediately.

00:27:39.722 --> 00:27:41.483
Good, said Richard.

00:27:41.543 --> 00:27:43.264
I want to see him, too.

00:27:43.324 --> 00:27:45.554
I have a lot of things to ask him.

00:27:45.615 --> 00:27:48.676
There are too many mysteries at Motehouse Castle.

00:27:48.736 --> 00:27:51.217
Too many things I don't understand.

00:27:51.277 --> 00:27:54.068
Sir Daniel is not telling me the truth.

00:27:54.128 --> 00:27:58.175
Richard, said Hatch, please be careful.

00:27:58.235 --> 00:28:02.152
Don't ask Sir Daniel's certain questions.

00:28:02.212 --> 00:28:04.112
What do you mean, Hatch?

00:28:04.172 --> 00:28:05.422
asked Richard.

00:28:05.482 --> 00:28:18.248
Well, you know, certain questions about, I want answers to my questions, said Richard angrily, and he went to Sir Daniel's room.

00:28:18.308 --> 00:28:20.578
Sir Oliver was there.

00:28:20.638 --> 00:28:25.608
He was sitting in a corner of the room, and his face was white.

00:28:25.668 --> 00:28:29.018
Come in, Richard," said Sir Daniel.

00:28:29.078 --> 00:28:30.879
Please sit down.

00:28:30.939 --> 00:28:33.820
You look worried, my boy.

00:28:33.880 --> 00:28:38.542
Are you still thinking about that letter on the church door?

00:28:38.602 --> 00:28:42.124
Yes, and I want some answers, said Richard.

00:28:42.184 --> 00:28:44.645
My father was killed when I was a little boy.

00:28:44.705 --> 00:28:47.816
People say that you and Sir Oliver killed him.

00:28:47.876 --> 00:28:50.471
I want to know the truth.

00:28:50.532 --> 00:28:56.939
Oh, Richard, do you really think I killed your father?

00:28:56.999 --> 00:28:59.220
Said Sir Daniel, smiling.

00:28:59.280 --> 00:29:02.182
Your father was my friend!

00:29:02.242 --> 00:29:08.935
When he died, I looked after you all these years and taught you many things.

00:29:08.996 --> 00:29:11.984
And poor Sir Oliver!

00:29:12.044 --> 00:29:16.763
He's a priest, a kind, honest man.

00:29:16.823 --> 00:29:21.878
Sir Daniel, for many years you used my family's money because I live with you.

00:29:21.938 --> 00:29:23.509
Said Richard angrily.

00:29:23.569 --> 00:29:26.932
And you'll soon plan my marriage and get a lot of money for it.

00:29:26.992 --> 00:29:29.934
How can you say these terrible things?

00:29:29.994 --> 00:29:31.215
Cried, Sir Daniel.

00:29:31.275 --> 00:29:34.508
You're making me very angry.

00:29:34.568 --> 00:29:36.670
But you're still a boy.

00:29:36.730 --> 00:29:39.652
We'll talk about this when you're a man.

00:29:39.712 --> 00:29:41.062
Remember.

00:29:41.122 --> 00:29:44.181
I did not kill your father.

00:29:44.241 --> 00:29:46.052
I promise."

00:29:46.112 --> 00:29:52.524
When Sir Oliver heard the words, I promise he jumped in his chair.

00:29:52.584 --> 00:29:56.705
Richard saw this and understood a lot.

00:29:56.765 --> 00:30:04.158
After he left the room, Sir Daniel said, the boy asks too many questions.

00:30:04.218 --> 00:30:07.568
He knows too many things.

00:30:07.628 --> 00:30:12.086
Put him in the room above the church.

00:30:12.146 --> 00:30:17.386
The room above the church asked Sir Oliver quietly.

00:30:17.446 --> 00:30:21.418
Yes, you heard me, said Sir Daniel.

00:30:21.479 --> 00:30:26.952
Richard went to his room and remembered Hatch's words.

00:30:27.012 --> 00:30:31.604
Don't trust Sir Daniel or Sir Oliver.

00:30:31.664 --> 00:30:39.119
In the evening, one of Sir Daniel's men came to his room and said, Follow me, Master Shelton.

00:30:39.179 --> 00:30:41.781
You'll sleep in another room tonight.

00:30:41.841 --> 00:30:43.183
In another room?

00:30:43.242 --> 00:30:44.354
asked Richard.

00:30:44.414 --> 00:30:47.636
Yes, in the room above the church.

00:30:47.656 --> 00:30:49.338
I said the man.

00:30:49.398 --> 00:30:54.452
It's nice and big, but it's full of ghosts.

00:30:54.512 --> 00:30:56.514
Full of ghosts?

00:30:56.574 --> 00:30:57.635
Thought Richard.

00:30:57.695 --> 00:30:59.580
What does he mean?

00:30:59.640 --> 00:31:05.296
Richard sat on the big bed in the new room, and he was worried.

00:31:05.356 --> 00:31:09.850
He did not know that many men were killed in that room.

00:31:09.910 --> 00:31:13.672
I must leave this castle immediately, he thought.

00:31:13.732 --> 00:31:16.194
Something bad is happening.

00:31:16.254 --> 00:31:20.377
Suddenly, someone knocked on the door.

00:31:20.437 --> 00:31:23.289
It was John Matcham.

00:31:23.350 --> 00:31:27.324
John, I'm happy to see you, said Richard.

00:31:27.384 --> 00:31:29.688
Oh, Richard, listen to me.

00:31:29.748 --> 00:31:30.759
Said John.

00:31:30.819 --> 00:31:33.250
I heard Sir Daniel's men talking.

00:31:33.310 --> 00:31:34.941
They want to kill you.

00:31:35.001 --> 00:31:37.112
I want to help you escape.

00:31:37.172 --> 00:31:40.514
I think there's a secret way out of this room.

00:31:40.574 --> 00:31:46.227
They started looking for it and found a small trap door under a table.

00:31:46.287 --> 00:31:48.568
This is the secret way out.

00:31:48.628 --> 00:31:50.259
Said John excitedly.

00:31:50.319 --> 00:31:52.300
We can escape together.

00:31:52.360 --> 00:31:55.224
Then they heard Sir Daniel's voice.

00:31:55.284 --> 00:31:59.208
Joanna, Joanna, where are you?

00:31:59.268 --> 00:32:01.168
Who is Joanna?

00:32:01.228 --> 00:32:02.878
asked Richard.

00:32:02.938 --> 00:32:08.539
John looked at Richard and said, I am Joanna.

00:32:08.599 --> 00:32:10.190
You?

00:32:10.250 --> 00:32:12.410
said Richard, surprised.

00:32:12.470 --> 00:32:14.110
Then you're not a boy.

00:32:14.170 --> 00:32:15.580
You're a girl.

00:32:15.640 --> 00:32:17.951
You're Joanna, sadly.

00:32:18.011 --> 00:32:21.432
Yes, I'm Joanna, sadly.

00:32:21.492 --> 00:32:23.952
She took off her big hat.

00:32:24.012 --> 00:32:27.632
and Richard could see her long blonde hair.

00:32:27.692 --> 00:32:29.303
She was very pretty.

00:32:29.323 --> 00:32:34.145
"'You're a brave girl,' said Richard, smiling.

00:32:34.165 --> 00:32:36.786
"'And you're beautiful, too.'

00:32:36.846 --> 00:32:39.467
They could hear Sir Daniel's voice again.

00:32:39.487 --> 00:32:41.238
"'Joanna!

00:32:41.298 --> 00:32:42.568
Where are you?'

00:32:42.588 --> 00:32:47.010
"'We must escape immediately,' said Joanna.

00:32:47.070 --> 00:32:52.422
They opened the trap-door and went down the long secret corridor.

00:32:52.482 --> 00:32:56.463
They came to a big door, but it was locked.

00:32:56.523 --> 00:32:58.374
What can we do now?

00:32:58.434 --> 00:32:59.734
Ask Joanna.

00:32:59.794 --> 00:33:02.276
I don't know, said Richard.

00:33:02.336 --> 00:33:06.327
Perhaps someone will open this door because we're near the church.

00:33:06.387 --> 00:33:08.418
Let's wait here.

00:33:08.478 --> 00:33:11.779
They sat down on the stone floor.

00:33:11.839 --> 00:33:14.710
Are you Sir Daniel's ward too?

00:33:14.770 --> 00:33:16.081
asked Richard.

00:33:16.141 --> 00:33:21.910
Yes, my mother and father are dead, and my family was rich.

00:33:21.971 --> 00:33:25.320
At first, Lord Foxham looked after me.

00:33:25.380 --> 00:33:27.221
He was a good man.

00:33:27.282 --> 00:33:29.724
Then Sir Daniel took me.

00:33:29.784 --> 00:33:33.966
After some time, Lord Foxham took me back.

00:33:34.027 --> 00:33:37.029
He wanted me to marry Lord Hamley.

00:33:37.089 --> 00:33:41.932
When Sir Daniel heard this, he decided to kidnap me.

00:33:41.992 --> 00:33:48.008
He gave me these boys clothes and said, You will marry Richard Shelton.

00:33:48.068 --> 00:33:52.218
Every marriage brings Sir Daniel a lot of money.

00:33:52.278 --> 00:33:56.207
I'm happy I met you, Joanna," said Richard.

00:33:56.267 --> 00:33:57.688
I am too.

00:33:57.748 --> 00:33:59.198
She said.

00:33:59.259 --> 00:34:03.582
Suddenly, they realized someone was behind them.

00:34:03.642 --> 00:34:05.842
It was Bennett Hatch.

00:34:05.903 --> 00:34:08.544
Hatch, what are you doing here?

00:34:08.604 --> 00:34:10.645
asked Richard, surprised.

00:34:10.706 --> 00:34:12.596
I'm looking for you, Richard.

00:34:12.656 --> 00:34:13.737
Said Hatch.

00:34:13.797 --> 00:34:17.380
Sir Daniel wants to kill you, but not Joanna.

00:34:17.440 --> 00:34:19.931
I want to help you both escape.

00:34:19.991 --> 00:34:22.574
Here is the key to the door.

00:34:22.634 --> 00:34:28.366
He took an old key from his pocket and opened the big door.

00:34:28.426 --> 00:34:32.257
Now you can escape across the church to the tower.

00:34:32.317 --> 00:34:35.438
I'll tell Sir Daniel I couldn't find you.

00:34:35.498 --> 00:34:38.618
Good luck.

00:34:38.678 --> 00:34:43.250
Listening activity.

00:34:43.309 --> 00:34:47.511
My parents died when I was only twelve.

00:34:47.571 --> 00:34:49.208
How did they die?

00:34:49.268 --> 00:34:53.438
There was a terrible fire at my home, Crombie Hall.

00:34:53.498 --> 00:34:55.439
Oh, how awful.

00:34:55.499 --> 00:34:56.910
What happened?

00:34:56.970 --> 00:34:59.462
Only I escaped the fire.

00:34:59.522 --> 00:35:04.856
After that, Lord Foxham, a good friend of my father, looked after me.

00:35:04.916 --> 00:35:10.909
Then one day, Sir Daniel invited us to a party at Mothouse Castle.

00:35:10.970 --> 00:35:15.866
We went, and Sir Daniel asked me to stay for a few weeks.

00:35:15.926 --> 00:35:19.723
I stayed, but then he didn't let me leave.

00:35:19.783 --> 00:35:21.864
How did you get away from him?

00:35:21.924 --> 00:35:24.877
Lord Foxham came with his soldiers.

00:35:24.937 --> 00:35:27.909
He ordered Sir Richard to let me go.

00:35:27.970 --> 00:35:29.921
Some years passed.

00:35:29.981 --> 00:35:33.154
Lord Foxham wanted me to marry Lord Hamley.

00:35:33.214 --> 00:35:34.424
Hamley?

00:35:34.484 --> 00:35:35.866
But why?

00:35:35.926 --> 00:35:38.638
He was a good friend of Lord Foxham.

00:35:38.698 --> 00:35:41.834
Lord Foxham thought I would be happy with him.

00:35:41.894 --> 00:35:45.700
Hamley was a good man, but very old.

00:35:45.760 --> 00:35:48.021
I didn't want to marry him.

00:35:48.081 --> 00:35:49.982
Then what happened?

00:35:50.042 --> 00:35:55.215
Well, then Sir Daniel came one day with three of his soldiers.

00:35:55.275 --> 00:36:01.908
I was in the garden at Lord Foxham's house when they came and kidnapped me.

00:36:01.968 --> 00:36:14.822
Chapter 5 Ellis Duckworth Richard and Joanna ran across the church to the castle tower.

00:36:14.882 --> 00:36:18.994
Richard tied the rope around a big stone.

00:36:19.054 --> 00:36:22.565
He looked back and saw no one.

00:36:22.625 --> 00:36:28.227
We must climb down the tower to the moat and swim to the other side, he said.

00:36:28.287 --> 00:36:31.348
Then we can run to the forest and we'll be free.

00:36:31.408 --> 00:36:34.809
Very well, said Joanna, bravely.

00:36:34.869 --> 00:36:38.490
I'll go first, and you can follow me," said Richard.

00:36:38.550 --> 00:36:40.571
Can you climb down a rope, Joanna?

00:36:40.631 --> 00:36:41.652
I'll try.

00:36:41.712 --> 00:36:43.172
She said.

00:36:43.232 --> 00:36:47.074
Richard started climbing down the rope.

00:36:47.134 --> 00:36:51.337
One of Sir Daniel's men on the other tower saw him.

00:36:51.398 --> 00:36:54.009
Shelton's trying to escape!

00:36:54.069 --> 00:36:55.449
He shouted.

00:36:55.510 --> 00:36:59.522
He shot Richard in the arm with an arrow.

00:36:59.582 --> 00:37:04.981
Richard fell into the moat and tried to swim to the other side.

00:37:05.041 --> 00:37:08.960
arrows were flying from the tower into the moat.

00:37:09.020 --> 00:37:14.764
When Joanna saw Richard falling into the moat, she screamed.

00:37:14.824 --> 00:37:19.718
One of Sir Daniel's men heard her and took her by the arm.

00:37:19.779 --> 00:37:23.762
She was Sir Daniel's prisoner again.

00:37:23.822 --> 00:37:28.896
Richard got out of the water and ran into the forest.

00:37:28.956 --> 00:37:34.886
From there he could see Mothouse Castle, but he could not see Joanna.

00:37:34.946 --> 00:37:38.991
One of Sir Daniel's men probably caught her, he thought.

00:37:39.051 --> 00:37:43.322
But Sir Daniel won't hurt her, because he wants to plan her marriage.

00:37:43.382 --> 00:37:46.322
I'll come back and rescue her soon.

00:37:46.382 --> 00:37:50.113
His arm hurt, and he could not walk.

00:37:50.173 --> 00:37:53.484
He fell to the ground on the leaves.

00:37:53.544 --> 00:37:58.525
Ellis Duckworth and another man found Richard the next morning.

00:37:58.585 --> 00:38:03.793
He was very ill, so they took him to an inn and put him to bed.

00:38:03.853 --> 00:38:11.482
When Richard woke up, he said, oh, my arm and head hurt a lot.

00:38:11.542 --> 00:38:15.364
Ellis Duckworth took his hand and smiled.

00:38:15.424 --> 00:38:21.796
My dear boy, I'm Ellis Duckworth, and I was your father's best friend.

00:38:21.856 --> 00:38:24.677
He was like a brother to me.

00:38:24.737 --> 00:38:31.129
He looked at the other man and said, he's lawless, one of my best men.

00:38:31.189 --> 00:38:34.746
Now, Richard, please sleep.

00:38:34.806 --> 00:38:39.796
When you're better, you'll tell me your story and will help you."

00:38:39.856 --> 00:38:47.182
The next day, Richard was feeling better, and he told Ellis Duckworth his long story.

00:38:47.202 --> 00:38:50.985
"'I'm happy you're here with us,' said Ellis.

00:38:51.005 --> 00:38:57.420
"'We're the band of the Black Arrow, and we want to punish bad people.

00:38:57.480 --> 00:39:00.670
I know you're brave and loyal, Richard.

00:39:00.730 --> 00:39:07.270
Together, we'll fight and destroy, Sir Daniel, and we'll rescue Joanna too.

00:39:07.330 --> 00:39:11.382
But first, we must find out where she is.

00:39:11.442 --> 00:39:19.186
A few days later, a mysterious messenger took this letter to Mothouse Castle.

00:39:19.246 --> 00:39:25.000
To Sir Daniel Brackley, you are a bad man.

00:39:25.060 --> 00:39:28.338
You are greedy and dishonest.

00:39:28.398 --> 00:39:31.644
Now I know you killed my father.

00:39:31.705 --> 00:39:35.308
One day, I will kill you.

00:39:35.368 --> 00:39:38.350
Leave Joanna, sadly alone.

00:39:38.410 --> 00:39:41.092
I want to marry her soon.

00:39:41.152 --> 00:39:43.964
Richard Shelton.

00:39:44.024 --> 00:39:51.008
Sir Daniel read the letter and thought, that boy is dangerous.

00:39:51.068 --> 00:39:53.390
I must find him.

00:39:53.451 --> 00:39:57.866
Many months passed, and it was already winter.

00:39:57.926 --> 00:40:03.992
The house of Lancaster won a lot of battles and became strong and important.

00:40:04.053 --> 00:40:07.295
York was very weak now.

00:40:07.356 --> 00:40:13.220
The town of Shorby on the hill was full of Lancaster nobles.

00:40:13.281 --> 00:40:21.207
Sir Daniel with sixty men, his friend Lord Shorby with two hundred men, and many others.

00:40:21.267 --> 00:40:24.730
One cold winter night in January.

00:40:24.790 --> 00:40:29.692
Three men of the band of the black arrows sat in a dark inn.

00:40:29.752 --> 00:40:33.333
I don't like this place, said one man.

00:40:33.393 --> 00:40:36.094
There are two many enemies here.

00:40:36.154 --> 00:40:41.466
We're here to help Master Shelton, said Lawless.

00:40:41.526 --> 00:40:45.477
Suddenly a young man came into the inn.

00:40:45.537 --> 00:40:47.208
Master Shelton?

00:40:47.268 --> 00:40:48.298
said Lawless.

00:40:48.358 --> 00:40:52.561
So Daniel left the inn a few minutes ago with six men.

00:40:52.621 --> 00:40:56.394
Let's follow him," said Richard.

00:40:56.454 --> 00:41:03.875
It was dark outside, but they could see Sir Daniel and his men walking towards the sea.

00:41:03.936 --> 00:41:08.787
Near the sea they saw an old lord with some men.

00:41:08.847 --> 00:41:11.018
He was short and fat.

00:41:11.078 --> 00:41:15.778
He met Sir Daniel in front of a stone house with a wall around it.

00:41:15.838 --> 00:41:21.776
Richard and his men hid behind some trees and watched the two men.

00:41:21.836 --> 00:41:24.513
But they could not hear them speak.

00:41:24.573 --> 00:41:27.154
It's old Lord Shorby.

00:41:27.214 --> 00:41:28.934
Thought Richard angrily.

00:41:28.994 --> 00:41:31.494
He's another greedy man.

00:41:31.554 --> 00:41:36.926
Tell me, Sir Daniel, how is the young girl?

00:41:36.986 --> 00:41:39.026
Ask the old lord.

00:41:39.086 --> 00:41:42.066
Is she very beautiful?

00:41:42.126 --> 00:41:44.017
Lord Shorby.

00:41:44.077 --> 00:41:45.297
Said Sir Daniel.

00:41:45.357 --> 00:41:51.420
Joanna Segley's young, beautiful, and very rich.

00:41:51.480 --> 00:41:54.324
She'll be an excellent wife.

00:41:54.384 --> 00:41:59.088
The Sedley family was very rich and very important.

00:41:59.149 --> 00:42:01.840
She'll bring you a lot of money.

00:42:01.900 --> 00:42:08.416
And I'll pay you a lot of money, Sir Daniel, but I want to see her now."

00:42:08.476 --> 00:42:10.578
said Lord Shorby.

00:42:10.638 --> 00:42:16.808
Sir Daniel and Lord Shorby went into the Stone House, followed by their men.

00:42:16.868 --> 00:42:22.416
When they came out, Lord Shorby was smiling and went home.

00:42:22.476 --> 00:42:26.570
Sir Daniel and his men went back to the inn.

00:42:26.630 --> 00:42:33.925
Now we know Joanna is Sir Daniel's prisoner, said Richard, and Lord Shorby wants to marry her.

00:42:33.985 --> 00:42:36.146
That greedy old man.

00:42:36.206 --> 00:42:38.488
We must stop this marriage.

00:42:38.549 --> 00:42:41.020
I want to look inside of the house.

00:42:41.080 --> 00:42:43.212
Lawless, come with me please.

00:42:43.272 --> 00:42:45.541
The others can wait here.

00:42:45.601 --> 00:42:49.830
Richard climbed to the top of the stone wall.

00:42:49.890 --> 00:42:54.802
From there he could see the kitchen window and Joanna.

00:42:54.862 --> 00:43:02.926
She was sitting at a table with Bennett Hatch's wife, and three of Sir Daniel's men stood behind her.

00:43:02.986 --> 00:43:07.058
She's very beautiful, thought Richard.

00:43:07.118 --> 00:43:12.882
He was happy to see her, but he was angry with Sir Daniel and Lord Shorby.

00:43:12.942 --> 00:43:17.958
He climbed down the wall and said to his men, I saw Joanna.

00:43:18.018 --> 00:43:19.639
She's inside.

00:43:19.699 --> 00:43:21.540
We must rescue her.

00:43:21.600 --> 00:43:25.634
Let's think of a good plan.

00:43:25.694 --> 00:43:42.840
Chapter 6 The Two Friars Richard and the men of the Black Arrow decided to attack Sir Daniel's house near the sea and rescue Joanna.

00:43:42.900 --> 00:43:49.659
That night, Richard and his twenty men climbed over the wall of the house.

00:43:49.719 --> 00:43:54.720
But Sir Daniel's men attacked them before they could get into the house.

00:43:54.780 --> 00:44:00.082
Sir Daniel had sixty men, and Richard had only twenty.

00:44:00.142 --> 00:44:06.854
His men fought bravely, but they could not get into the house and rescue Joanna.

00:44:06.914 --> 00:44:11.285
Many men were hurt, and some were killed.

00:44:11.345 --> 00:44:14.668
They went back to the forest.

00:44:14.728 --> 00:44:23.197
When Sir Daniel heard about the attack, he said, Shelton wants to rescue Joanna and marry her.

00:44:23.257 --> 00:44:26.570
We must take her to my castle in Shorby.

00:44:26.630 --> 00:44:31.804
She'll be safe there, and she'll marry Lord Shorby in a few days.

00:44:31.864 --> 00:44:37.058
The next morning, Richard and Lawless sat by the fire.

00:44:37.118 --> 00:44:44.054
If we don't rescue Joanna, she'll have to marry that old Lord, said Richard sadly.

00:44:44.114 --> 00:44:46.055
What can we do?

00:44:46.115 --> 00:44:51.656
Lawless looked at him and said, perhaps I can help you.

00:44:51.716 --> 00:44:53.446
Follow me.

00:44:53.506 --> 00:44:55.227
Where are we going?

00:44:55.287 --> 00:45:00.258
asked Richard, to a secret place, said Lawless.

00:45:00.318 --> 00:45:05.309
They walked in the snow to a small den under a big tree.

00:45:05.369 --> 00:45:10.720
Inside the den there was a table and a wooden box.

00:45:10.780 --> 00:45:14.562
This is my secret den, said Lawless.

00:45:14.622 --> 00:45:18.224
Your secret den, said Richard, surprised.

00:45:18.284 --> 00:45:20.176
It's very small.

00:45:20.236 --> 00:45:25.890
Lawless opened the wooden box and took out a friar's robe.

00:45:25.950 --> 00:45:28.331
It was old and brown.

00:45:28.391 --> 00:45:31.002
Then he took out another one.

00:45:31.062 --> 00:45:32.784
What are these?

00:45:32.844 --> 00:45:34.085
asked Richard.

00:45:34.145 --> 00:45:36.416
They're two friar's robes.

00:45:36.476 --> 00:45:40.969
Let's put them on, and everyone will think we're friars.

00:45:41.030 --> 00:45:42.650
But why?

00:45:42.710 --> 00:45:45.035
asked Richard, confused.

00:45:45.095 --> 00:45:49.659
With these robes, no one will recognize us," said Lawless.

00:45:49.719 --> 00:45:53.310
We can easily get into Sir Daniel's castle in Shorby.

00:45:53.370 --> 00:45:56.950
Remember, no one stops a fryer.

00:45:57.010 --> 00:45:59.841
Sir Daniel's castle in Shorby.

00:45:59.901 --> 00:46:01.211
But why?

00:46:01.271 --> 00:46:02.731
asked Richard.

00:46:02.791 --> 00:46:04.812
Master Shelton.

00:46:04.872 --> 00:46:05.962
cried Lawless.

00:46:06.022 --> 00:46:11.343
Joanna is now in his castle, and she'll soon marry old Lord Shorby.

00:46:11.403 --> 00:46:13.590
Now do you understand?

00:46:13.650 --> 00:46:16.346
Richard was very surprised.

00:46:16.406 --> 00:46:17.997
How do you know this?

00:46:18.057 --> 00:46:19.237
He asked.

00:46:19.297 --> 00:46:24.238
Young man, I'm lawless, and I'm much older than you.

00:46:24.298 --> 00:46:27.459
I know a lot of things you don't know.

00:46:27.519 --> 00:46:30.229
But how can we stop this marriage?

00:46:30.289 --> 00:46:31.680
Asked Richard.

00:46:31.740 --> 00:46:34.910
We'll think of a plan, said lawless.

00:46:34.970 --> 00:46:38.151
Now, put on the fryer's robe.

00:46:38.211 --> 00:46:41.912
Richard put on the robe and asked.

00:46:41.972 --> 00:46:44.047
How do I look?

00:46:44.107 --> 00:46:50.976
Not bad, but I must do something to your face now," answered Laulus.

00:46:51.036 --> 00:46:58.392
He took some dark pencils from the box and drew a moustache and a small beard on Richard's young face.

00:46:58.412 --> 00:47:03.756
"'Perfect," he said, "'now you look like a friar.

00:47:03.817 --> 00:47:09.310
Remember to keep your hood on, and no one will recognize you.'"

00:47:09.370 --> 00:47:14.806
Laulus put on the other robe, and they left the den.

00:47:14.866 --> 00:47:19.260
When they got to Shorby, they went to the castle.

00:47:19.321 --> 00:47:30.266
There were a lot of people at the castle, rich gentlemen with their ladies, soldiers, merchants, musicians and acrobats.

00:47:30.326 --> 00:47:37.270
The two friars went to a soldier and said, We're here to visit Joanna saidley.

00:47:37.330 --> 00:47:41.963
Her room is on the second floor, said the soldier.

00:47:42.023 --> 00:47:47.797
The two friars went to the second floor and found Joanna's room.

00:47:47.857 --> 00:47:51.480
I'll wait outside, said Lawless.

00:47:51.540 --> 00:47:56.683
Richard entered Joanna's room and took off his hood.

00:47:56.744 --> 00:47:58.265
Joanna?

00:47:58.325 --> 00:47:59.956
He said softly.

00:48:00.016 --> 00:48:02.558
It's me, Richard.

00:48:02.618 --> 00:48:05.751
She ran to him and they hugged.

00:48:05.811 --> 00:48:07.362
Oh, Richard?

00:48:07.422 --> 00:48:10.634
Joanna said, I'm happy to see you.

00:48:10.694 --> 00:48:12.570
What are you doing here?

00:48:12.630 --> 00:48:16.276
I'm here with a friend to rescue you," said Richard.

00:48:16.336 --> 00:48:17.366
But how?

00:48:17.426 --> 00:48:18.757
Joanna asked.

00:48:18.817 --> 00:48:24.018
I'm Sir Daniel's prisoner, and I have to marry Lord Shorby tomorrow morning.

00:48:24.078 --> 00:48:28.279
I'm so unhappy because I don't want to marry him.

00:48:28.339 --> 00:48:31.930
You won't marry that horrible old man, said Richard.

00:48:31.990 --> 00:48:33.260
I promise, Joanna.

00:48:33.321 --> 00:48:35.191
I want to marry you.

00:48:35.251 --> 00:48:39.480
He put on his hood and left the room quietly.

00:48:39.540 --> 00:48:43.529
He and Lawless went to the church to think of a plan.

00:48:43.589 --> 00:48:48.070
But Richard met Sir Oliver in the church.

00:48:48.130 --> 00:48:52.782
Richard Shelton, he said, surprised.

00:48:52.842 --> 00:48:55.163
Sir Daniel is looking for you.

00:48:55.223 --> 00:48:57.234
You're in great danger.

00:48:57.294 --> 00:49:00.815
I'm here to stop Joanna's marriage, said Richard.

00:49:00.875 --> 00:49:03.096
I'm not afraid of Sir Daniel.

00:49:03.156 --> 00:49:09.824
You can't stop this marriage, said the priest, because Sir Daniel will kill you.

00:49:09.884 --> 00:49:14.894
You must stay in this church until tomorrow morning and then leave.

00:49:14.954 --> 00:49:19.917
If you try to escape, I'll call the soldiers.

00:49:19.977 --> 00:49:24.460
Richard and Lawless could not move.

00:49:24.520 --> 00:49:29.884
At nine o'clock the next morning, there were a lot of people in the church.

00:49:29.944 --> 00:49:33.055
Richard and Lawless were there too.

00:49:33.115 --> 00:49:39.600
Joanna was wearing a beautiful white dress and had flowers in her hair.

00:49:39.660 --> 00:49:42.882
But she was pale and sad.

00:49:42.942 --> 00:49:48.107
Old Lord Shorby was wearing his best clothes.

00:49:48.167 --> 00:49:53.042
Joanna and Lord Shorby stood in front of the priest.

00:49:53.102 --> 00:49:58.326
Ellis Duckworth and his men were hiding on the stairs of the church tower.

00:49:58.386 --> 00:50:06.399
Suddenly a black arrow flew across the church and killed Lord Shorby.

00:50:06.459 --> 00:50:10.500
Joanna and the people in the church screamed.

00:50:10.560 --> 00:50:15.091
Sir Daniel and his men took Joanna away immediately.

00:50:15.151 --> 00:50:19.942
Richard and Lawless were angry, but they could do nothing.

00:50:20.002 --> 00:50:26.530
They watched Joanna leave with Sir Daniel.

00:50:26.590 --> 00:50:32.680
The victory of York.

00:50:32.740 --> 00:50:37.741
Richard and Lawless returned to the forest.

00:50:37.801 --> 00:50:43.483
That night, Ellis Duckworth's men sat around the fire.

00:50:43.543 --> 00:50:51.266
There's going to be an important battle tomorrow between the houses of Lancaster and York, said Duckworth to his men.

00:50:51.326 --> 00:50:54.077
We're going to attack Shorby Castle.

00:50:54.137 --> 00:50:56.278
This time, York will win.

00:50:56.298 --> 00:50:57.978
Hooray!

00:50:58.038 --> 00:50:59.348
Cried the men.

00:50:59.408 --> 00:51:02.919
And we're going to find my enemy, Sir Daniel.

00:51:02.979 --> 00:51:09.961
Remember, there's a black arrow waiting for him and his good friends, Bennett Hatch and Sir Oliver Oates.

00:51:10.021 --> 00:51:12.182
We'll find them!

00:51:12.242 --> 00:51:13.612
Cried the man.

00:51:13.672 --> 00:51:15.813
Richard, said Duckworth.

00:51:15.873 --> 00:51:20.154
Go and meet the Duke of Gloucester at St Bridget's Cross tomorrow morning.

00:51:20.214 --> 00:51:23.105
Take him this important message.

00:51:23.165 --> 00:51:33.220
Dear Richard, Duke of Gloucester, My twenty men will meet your soldiers outside Shorby Castle before the battle.

00:51:33.280 --> 00:51:36.534
We will fight together and win.

00:51:36.594 --> 00:51:38.656
Ellis Duckworth.

00:51:38.716 --> 00:51:44.563
Very early the next morning, Richard rode to St. Bridget's Cross.

00:51:44.623 --> 00:51:49.746
It was a cold morning and there was a lot of snow on the road.

00:51:49.806 --> 00:51:56.294
When he got there, he saw a young knight dressed in armour on a big black horse.

00:51:56.354 --> 00:52:00.835
The white rose at the house of York was on his shield.

00:52:00.895 --> 00:52:05.196
He was alone, and he was fighting eight soldiers.

00:52:05.256 --> 00:52:09.146
He was a good fighter, and killed three soldiers.

00:52:09.166 --> 00:52:12.437
"'I can help you, sir,' cried Richard.

00:52:12.497 --> 00:52:17.876
He and the knight fought together, and the fight was soon over.

00:52:17.936 --> 00:52:20.845
The young knight was surprised.

00:52:20.905 --> 00:52:25.116
He turned to Richard and said, Thank you for your help.

00:52:25.176 --> 00:52:28.337
You're a good fighter, and you saved my life.

00:52:28.397 --> 00:52:29.577
Who are you?

00:52:29.637 --> 00:52:33.418
I'm Richard Shelton, and I'm looking for the Duke of Gloucester.

00:52:33.478 --> 00:52:35.489
Well, you found him.

00:52:35.549 --> 00:52:36.650
Said the knight.

00:52:36.710 --> 00:52:39.210
I'm Richard, Duke of Gloucester.

00:52:39.270 --> 00:52:41.901
Here's a message from Ellis Duckworth.

00:52:41.961 --> 00:52:45.280
Said Richard, giving him the letter.

00:52:45.340 --> 00:52:50.052
The Duke read the letter and said, Good.

00:52:50.112 --> 00:52:53.045
I need more brave men for this battle.

00:52:53.105 --> 00:52:57.710
Duckworth is a loyal friend, and together we'll win.

00:52:57.770 --> 00:53:01.123
Soon the Duke's soldiers arrived.

00:53:01.183 --> 00:53:05.138
They were carrying flags with the white rose of York.

00:53:05.198 --> 00:53:06.438
We're ready!

00:53:06.498 --> 00:53:07.489
He cried.

00:53:07.550 --> 00:53:08.661
Let's attack!

00:53:08.721 --> 00:53:10.730
Sure be castle!

00:53:10.790 --> 00:53:17.269
Many of the soldiers at Shorbi Castle were still sleeping when the Duke attacked.

00:53:17.329 --> 00:53:23.081
Hundreds of soldiers fought in a long battle and many were killed.

00:53:23.141 --> 00:53:30.293
At the end of the battle there was a fire and Shorbi Castle was almost destroyed.

00:53:30.353 --> 00:53:39.757
The House of York won the battle and Sir Daniel escaped with Joanna, Bennett Hatch and two men.

00:53:39.817 --> 00:53:44.120
The Duke of Gloucester was pleased with the victory.

00:53:44.180 --> 00:53:51.254
He went to Richard and said, You're a brave young man and you fought well.

00:53:51.314 --> 00:53:53.386
Kneel down, Richard.

00:53:53.446 --> 00:53:55.716
I want to knight you.

00:53:55.776 --> 00:54:01.810
Richard knelt down in front of the Duke and became Sir Richard.

00:54:01.870 --> 00:54:05.236
This was a great honor for him.

00:54:05.296 --> 00:54:11.915
The next day, Sir Richard left Shorby and started looking for Joanna.

00:54:11.975 --> 00:54:14.947
He knew she was with Sir Daniel.

00:54:15.008 --> 00:54:21.402
He traveled all day and in the evening he saw a small fire on a hill.

00:54:21.462 --> 00:54:25.774
Perhaps that's Sir Daniel's fire, he thought.

00:54:25.834 --> 00:54:30.876
He moved silently through the trees and got closer.

00:54:30.937 --> 00:54:37.150
He saw Sir Daniel, Bennett Hatch, and a young boy sitting near the fire.

00:54:37.210 --> 00:54:39.684
They were eating and talking.

00:54:39.744 --> 00:54:44.087
Joanna is dressed as John Matcham again, thought Richard.

00:54:44.148 --> 00:54:47.251
Sir Daniel is very clever.

00:54:47.311 --> 00:54:52.136
Richard hid behind a big tree and watched them.

00:54:52.196 --> 00:54:56.090
It was obvious that Joanna was very sad.

00:54:56.150 --> 00:55:03.102
He waited until they were finally asleep, and then he quietly went up to Joanna.

00:55:03.163 --> 00:55:06.744
Joanna, he whispered in her ear.

00:55:06.804 --> 00:55:08.224
Wake up!

00:55:08.284 --> 00:55:11.146
She woke up and smiled.

00:55:11.206 --> 00:55:15.218
We must be very quiet, whispered Sir Richard.

00:55:15.278 --> 00:55:19.029
Get up slowly and follow me.

00:55:19.090 --> 00:55:23.612
They moved away very quietly through the trees.

00:55:23.672 --> 00:55:28.043
They got on Sir Richard's horse and went into the forest.

00:55:28.103 --> 00:55:33.904
That night, they slept at Ellis Duckworth's camp, near Holywood.

00:55:33.964 --> 00:55:39.656
When Joanna woke up, she said, This is like a dream, Richard.

00:55:39.716 --> 00:55:41.537
We're together again.

00:55:41.597 --> 00:55:46.328
Yes, and tomorrow we can get married, Sir Richard said excitedly.

00:55:46.388 --> 00:55:50.519
I'm going to talk to the kind friar of Holywood Abbey this morning.

00:55:50.579 --> 00:55:55.132
I'm very happy, Richard, said Joanna.

00:55:55.192 --> 00:56:01.059
Sir Richard woke up very early on the day of his marriage.

00:56:01.119 --> 00:56:04.852
He was the happiest man in the world.

00:56:04.912 --> 00:56:10.187
He put on his best clothes and took a short walk in the forest.

00:56:10.247 --> 00:56:14.260
Soon he saw a friar walking towards him.

00:56:14.321 --> 00:56:18.524
As the friar came closer, he recognized him.

00:56:18.584 --> 00:56:20.730
It was Sir Daniel.

00:56:20.790 --> 00:56:25.096
He put his hand on his sword because he was ready to fight.

00:56:25.156 --> 00:56:29.657
I'm not here to fight you, said Sir Daniel sadly.

00:56:29.717 --> 00:56:36.628
My men and I fought bravely, but we lost the battle against the House of York.

00:56:36.688 --> 00:56:42.299
It was a long, terrible battle, and now I have nothing.

00:56:42.359 --> 00:56:49.181
I lost my castle, my men, my money, my jewels.

00:56:49.241 --> 00:56:51.357
I lost everything.

00:56:51.417 --> 00:56:56.817
Now I must escape to France, where I still have some friends.

00:56:56.877 --> 00:56:59.489
I hope they can help me.

00:56:59.550 --> 00:57:06.956
Go to France, Sir Daniel, and don't come back, said Sir Richard, angrily.

00:57:07.016 --> 00:57:11.970
Sir Daniel turned around and continued walking in the forest.

00:57:12.030 --> 00:57:22.025
But, after a minute, a black arrow flew through the morning air and hit him in the heart.

00:57:22.085 --> 00:57:27.666
He fell to the ground, and Sir Richard ran to his side.

00:57:27.726 --> 00:57:29.658
Richard?

00:57:29.718 --> 00:57:31.690
He said quietly.

00:57:31.750 --> 00:57:36.042
Is the arrow black?

00:57:36.102 --> 00:57:39.444
Yes, it's black.

00:57:39.504 --> 00:57:41.396
Said Richard.

00:57:41.456 --> 00:57:47.090
Sir Daniel looked at him for the last time and died.

00:57:47.150 --> 00:57:49.112
I killed him.

00:57:49.172 --> 00:57:51.426
Said a voice in the forest.

00:57:51.486 --> 00:57:53.669
It was Ellis Duckworth.

00:57:53.729 --> 00:57:57.060
And yesterday I killed Bennett Hatch!

00:57:57.120 --> 00:58:01.202
He walked out of the forest and stood by Richard.

00:58:01.262 --> 00:58:05.935
You killed all of your enemies, except one, said Richard.

00:58:05.995 --> 00:58:10.478
Yes, so Oliver is still alive, said Duckworth.

00:58:10.538 --> 00:58:13.299
Don't kill him, Ellis, said Richard.

00:58:13.359 --> 00:58:15.740
Let's live in peace.

00:58:15.800 --> 00:58:19.420
Duckworth thought for a moment.

00:58:19.480 --> 00:58:24.681
He looked at the body of Sir Daniel and said, You're right, Richard.

00:58:24.741 --> 00:58:26.942
I want to live in peace.

00:58:27.002 --> 00:58:31.202
I don't want to fight or kill anymore.

00:58:31.263 --> 00:58:36.934
The band of the Black Arrow doesn't exist anymore.

00:58:36.994 --> 00:58:45.216
At nine o'clock that morning, Richard and Joanna finally got married at Holywood Abbey.

00:58:45.277 --> 00:58:49.890
It was a beautiful wedding, and everyone was happy.

00:58:49.950 --> 00:59:01.123
Richard, Joanna, Ellis Duckworth, the men of the Black Arrow, and the Duke of Gloucester and his soldiers, celebrated with a dinner.

00:59:01.184 --> 00:59:11.555
Richard and Joanna lived a happy, peaceful life in the forest, far from wars and battles.

00:59:11.615 --> 00:59:16.694
Knights and their knighthood today.

00:59:16.754 --> 00:59:24.780
Today, the title Knight refers to people who receive this honour from the King or Queen.

00:59:24.840 --> 00:59:29.512
It is a thank you for good services to the country.

00:59:29.572 --> 00:59:36.836
But in the Middle Ages, a knight was a soldier who fought for the King and the country.

00:59:36.896 --> 00:59:43.210
Knights in the Middle Ages almost always came from noble families.

00:59:43.270 --> 00:59:50.606
They had a high position in society and worked for lords or directly for the king.

00:59:50.666 --> 00:59:57.641
When they went into battle, they wore heavy armor and rode strong horses.

00:59:57.702 --> 01:00:05.578
They carried a special shield with their family symbol called a coat of arms.

01:00:05.638 --> 01:00:13.620
When they weren't fighting in battles, knights often practiced their skills by going to tournaments.

01:00:13.680 --> 01:00:22.163
These were big competitions, and there were several different sports, including jousting.

01:00:22.224 --> 01:00:27.217
Boys learnt how to become a knight from the age of seven.

01:00:27.278 --> 01:00:31.180
These young boys were called pages.

01:00:31.241 --> 01:00:37.486
They learnt about horses and armour and how to fight with a wooden sword.

01:00:37.546 --> 01:00:42.480
When they were around twelve, they became squires.

01:00:42.540 --> 01:00:47.074
A squire learned how to fight from a real knight.

01:00:47.134 --> 01:00:55.290
He also helped the knight do many things, including putting on his armour before going into battle.

01:00:55.350 --> 01:01:02.396
Today's knights do not need to fight, and they do not have a specific job to do.

01:01:02.456 --> 01:01:06.708
The special honour is called a knighthood.

01:01:06.768 --> 01:01:11.730
In Great Britain, these awards are given twice a year.

01:01:11.790 --> 01:01:19.050
If you are knighted by the Queen, you are then invited to a special ceremony at Buckingham Palace.

01:01:19.110 --> 01:01:26.542
Here you kneel in front of the Queen and she touches your shoulders with a sword.

01:01:26.602 --> 01:01:37.571
A British man can then use Sir before his name, and a British woman can use Dame before hers.

01:01:37.631 --> 01:01:44.192
Sometimes the Queen awards an honorary knighthood to non-British citizens.

01:01:44.252 --> 01:01:49.796
These people are knighted, but they cannot officially use the title.

01:01:49.857 --> 01:01:55.292
Recent examples are Bob Geldorf and Bill Gates.

01:01:55.352 --> 01:02:02.738
Often non-famous people are given a knighthood to say thank you for their charity work.

